","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/deployments","created_at":"2016-08-13T05:26:41Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T11:23:33Z","pushed_at":"2026-03-11T11:26:45Z","git_url":"git://github.com/pytorch/pytorch.git","ssh_url":"org-21003710@github.com:pytorch/pytorch.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch","homepage":"https://pytorch.org","size":1267772,"stargazers_count":98201,"watchers_count":98201,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":27143,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":18135,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["autograd","deep-learning","gpu","machine-learning","neural-network","numpy","python","tensor"],"visibility":"public","forks":27143,"open_issues":18135,"watchers":98201,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/pulls/161639","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/161639","diff_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/161639.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/161639.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fixes #161014 \r\n\r\nThis bug fix introduces a fix that is consistent with the exception handling. Outlined in issue #161014, there is an edge case where the negative padding does not make the tensor size negative but still triggers the exception that the size is negative. The fix is simply adding `new_dim >=0` to include the zero dim and letting the operator return an empty tensor.\r\n\r\nIn the PR I have added the edge case where the test will now check the negative padding where the dimension gets reduced to zero.  But the sample is only for the `constant` type of padding. I would like some feedback if it is necessary to put the same sample on the `reduce` type as well.\r\n\r\nThis is my first PR to contribute to PyTorch and any help/feedback will be welcome! Thank you!\r\n\r\n@malfet @manuelcandales @janeyx99 @ezyang\r\n\n\ncc @H-Huang @awgu @wanchaol @fegin @fduwjj @wz337 @wconstab @d4l3k @pragupta @ezyang @msaroufim @dcci @voznesenskym @penguinwu @EikanWang @jgong5 @Guobing-Chen @XiaobingSuper @zhuhaozhe @blzheng @wenzhe-nrv @jiayisunx @ipiszy @chenyang78 @kadeng @muchulee8 @amjames @chauhang @aakhundov @coconutruben @Lucaskabela","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/161639/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/161639/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3239213296","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/161014#issuecomment-3239213296","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/161014","id":3239213296,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87BEnjw","user":{"login":"PluvioXO","id":75335290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzM1Mjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75335290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO","html_url":"https://github.com/PluvioXO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-30T11:51:57Z","updated_at":"2025-08-30T11:51:57Z","body":"I can fix this by allowing zero-signed outputs when mixing negative and positive padding. E.g:\nx = torch.ones(5, 3)\ntorch.ops.aten.constant_pad_nd.default(x, [-1, -2, 1, 1])\nproduces an error even though W: 3 - 1 - 2 == 0 should be valid and the result should have shape (7, 0). Can fix by making size from from new_dim > 0 to new_dim >= 0. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3239213296/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"PluvioXO","id":75335290,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzM1Mjkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75335290?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO","html_url":"https://github.com/PluvioXO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PluvioXO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"p